hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2839","Narrated to us Ziyad ibn Ayyub, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said:\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: *\"Indeed, Allah (SWT) boasts to the people of the heavens about the people of Arafat, and He says to them: 'Look at My servants who have come to Me disheveled and dusty.'\"*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"2840","###\n Abu Bakr (RA) said: Marzuq (who is Abu Bakr) narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"On the Day of Arafah, Allah descends to the lowest heaven and boasts about them to the angels, saying: 'Look at My servants! They come to Me disheveled and dust-covered, having traveled from every deep pass.' He says: 'I call you to witness that I have"
